      "date": "2026-11-05 02:32:35.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 4:\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nLooks good; one optional test suggestion, no need to re-spin for it.\n\n(suggestion) If the patch is refreshed, consider a lock_prim_nid=1 case in sanity-lnet. The new -EEXIST also changes the default configuration: LNetAddPeer() passes flags 0 for every NID after the first, so a NID held as non-primary by an unlocked peer now goes through lnet_peer_force_merge() on that multi-NID peer instead of a recreated single-NID peer. test_40 covers a peer whose primary NID is the added NID, test_42 covers a new NID, and test_43 forces lock_prim_nid=0, so the merge the commit message describes for lock_prim_nid=1 is not exercised.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 4
    },
