          "date": "2026-11-03 04:13:34.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20635 lnet: adopt an existing unlocked peer",
        "message": "LU-20635 lnet: adopt an existing unlocked peer\n\nWith lock_prim_nid=0, a client mount can fail with -EIO. This\nfailure occurs when the server advertises a primary NID that is not\nthe mount NID.\n\nLNetAddPeer() adds the NIDs that Lustre knows for a node. When an\nunlocked peer holds one of these NIDs as a non-primary NID,\nlnet_peer_add() deletes that peer. It then makes the NID the primary\nNID of a new peer. Discovery can move the primary NID back, so the\nprimary NID of the node changes on each add. PtlRPC posts reply\nbuffers for the cached primary NID, so replies stop matching them.\n\nWhen the caller does not configure or lock the peer, adopt an\nexisting peer that is not CONFIGURED or LOCK_PRIMARY. Return -EEXIST.\nAt lock_prim_nid=1, LNetAddPeer() then merges that peer into the\nprimary peer, as LU-20439 requires.\n\nAdd sanity-lnet test_43 for the lock_prim_nid=0 case.\n\nFixes: fc7a0d6013b4 (\"LU-14668 lnet: add 'lock_prim_nid\" lnet module parameter\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5\nChange-Id: Ib797c3a17696f443e11ec7b4439409c2de9e7b28\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
